{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/798063-2e-conversion-the-death-clause","id":798063,"title":"[2E Conversion] The Death Clause","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-01T19:23:18-08:00","id":798063,"title":"[2E Conversion] The Death Clause","content":"Has anyone thought about converting (and perhaps improving the effectiveness of) the Death Clause from Book of the Dead? I've been thinking of tackling it, seeing as I haven't seen any threads covered on it here yet. Plus, it (and the Contract of Shade and Spirit) are worth using for Changeling/Sin-Eater crossovers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T19:31:03-08:00","id":798065,"title":"","content":"I might look it over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T21:13:13-08:00","id":798089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/798063-2e-conversion-the-death-clause?p=798065#post798065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might look it over.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> For the convenience of easy reference.... <hr /> <b>The Death Clause</b><br /> <br /> <br /> Upon entering the Underworld for the first time, a changeling feels as though she has taken part in a powerful pledge. The player rolls Clarity at this point (Darkling receives a +2 modifier).<br /> <br /> <i>Dramatic Failure:</i> The character is blind to the Death Clause, and does not enjoy its benefits, even if it is later explained to her. Something about her, perhaps something she did during her Durance, exempts her.<br /> <br /> <i>Failure:</i> The character does not perceive the Death Clause, and cannot take advantage of the benefit until he does. The player can make the Clarity roll once per day in the Underworld.<br /> <br /> <i>Success: </i>The character immediately becomes aware of the Death Clause, but the benefits must be discovered by investigation (probably talking to other changelings, or delving deep into the Underworld to learn the truth).<br /> <br /> <i>Exceptional Success:</i> The character immediately understands the Death Clause in full, including all benefits.<br /> <br /> The Death Clause is, as the name suggests, an ancient agreement between Faerie and the Underworld. The Gentry agreed they would be mortal, but that Death would not come for them until certain conditions were fulfilled. Every member of the Gentry, like so many other things fae, has a condition or a weapon that can fell him. Of course, since the Gentry choose their own methods of demise, these conditions are absurdly obscure, but they are all <i>possible</i>. Just knowing this gives the Lost a great deal of hope.<br /> <br /> The Death Clause has benefits for changelings as well, though. A changeling that buys into the Clause (which costs a <i>dot </i>of Willpower) \u201cpurchases\u201d one death. The character can die once and return to life in the Underworld, in a special cavern in the Autochthonous Depths. This does leave the character with the problem of finding her way back to the living world, but she is alive. The player can buy back the dot of Willpower with eight experience points, and a changeling can only ever take advantage of the Death Clause once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 01-02-2016, 11:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T21:52:39-08:00","id":798104,"title":"","content":"I have the book, thanks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T10:47:27-08:00","id":798315,"title":"","content":"And suddenly, I'm imagining modernized remakes of Orpheus' journey. Don't look back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T18:55:11-08:00","id":798546,"title":"","content":"What book is this from?","signature":"","edite